      <!-- ===================== UPGRADING & FULL DETAILS ===================== -->
      <div class="v28-reference" id="v2.8.0-upgrading">
        <div class="v28-ref-head">
          <span class="kicker">Upgrade &amp; reference</span>
          <h3>Before you upgrade to v2.8.0</h3>
        </div>

        <aside class="upgrade-note">
          <strong>This release requires downtime.</strong> Back up the metadata database, then stop every old replica before the first new one starts. Rolling upgrades are not supported: an old binary writes alert columns that no longer exist. Startup runs 18 migrations on each store (SQLite <code>000042</code> to <code>000059</code>, Postgres <code>000016</code> to <code>000033</code>). Treat them as forward-only: the alert migrations move each rule's targets into destinations and cannot be undone, so rolling back means restoring the backup.
          <ol class="upgrade-steps">
            <li>Remove <code>alerts.evaluation_interval</code> from config. Keep at least one replica with both <code>jobs.enabled = true</code> and <code>alerts.enabled = true</code>.</li>
            <li>Review <code>[audit]</code> limits: <code>retention_days</code> (default 30) and <code>max_rows</code> (default 1,000,000), which each <code>query.run</code> event counts toward.</li>
            <li>Verify SMTP in <strong>Administration &rarr; System Settings &rarr; Alerts</strong> if you send alert or report email.</li>
            <li>Reload open Logchef tabs, reissue explicitly scoped API tokens that need the new scopes, run <code>logchef auth</code> again for CLI views, and sign MCP clients in again for <code>list_saved_views</code>.</li>
            <li>Migrated webhooks stay on payload v1 with at-least-once delivery; deduplicate on <code>Logchef-Delivery-Id</code> and migrate receivers to v2 when ready.</li>
          </ol>
        </aside>

        <div class="change-section">
          <div class="change-type breaking">Breaking changes</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li><strong>No rolling upgrades</strong>: Stop every old replica before starting v2.8.0.</li>
            <li><strong>Alert API</strong>: Create or update requests containing <code>recipient_user_ids</code> or <code>webhook_urls</code> (even empty arrays) answer <code>400</code>. Create a destination at <code>POST /api/v1/notification-destinations</code> and pass its ID in <code>destination_ids</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Alert frequency</strong>: <code>frequency_seconds</code> below 10 answers <code>400</code>. Existing rules below 10 seconds run every 10 seconds.</li>
            <li><strong>Webhook test route removed</strong>: <code>POST /api/v1/admin/settings/test-webhook</code> is replaced by <code>POST /api/v1/notification-destinations/test</code>; inspect <code>data.ok</code> because HTTP 200 can report a failed delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>Config removed</strong>: <code>alerts.evaluation_interval</code> (and <code>LOGCHEF_ALERTS__EVALUATION_INTERVAL</code>) is removed.</li>
            <li><strong>Grouped notifications</strong>: Grouped rules send one notification per group to each destination type. Webhooks send <code>Logchef-Delivery-Id</code> with at-least-once delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>Query Activity API</strong>: <code>GET /api/v1/admin/query-activity</code> is removed; use <code>GET /api/v1/admin/query-stats</code> with <code>account</code>, <code>source_id</code> and <code>user_id</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>New token scopes</strong>: <code>saved_views:read</code>, <code>saved_views:write</code>, <code>destinations:read</code>, <code>destinations:write</code>, <code>reports:read</code>, <code>reports:write</code> and <code>audit:read</code>. Tokens with explicit scope lists need reissuing; full-access tokens are unaffected.</li>
            <li><strong>Team source links</strong>: Linking a source you cannot access fails as source not found. Global admins and provisioning are unaffected.</li>
            <li><strong>Provisioning export</strong>: Custom headers on VictoriaLogs and Loki sources export as <code>header_secret_refs</code> environment variable names; provisioning refuses to start when a referenced variable is unset or empty.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-section">
          <div class="change-type security">Security</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li><strong>Team source links need access</strong>: A team admin can link only a source they can already access. Before, a team admin could link any source and query its logs.</li>
            <li><strong>No header values in exports</strong>: Provisioning export names an environment variable for each custom header of a VictoriaLogs or Loki source instead of writing its value.</li>
            <li><strong>Quieter webhook failures</strong>: A failed delivery no longer writes the receiver's response body to the server log.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="change-section">
          <div class="change-type fixed">Fixed</div>
          <ul class="change-list">
            <li>Live tail frees its slot as soon as the client disconnects, on every backend.</li>
            <li>A dashboard of 4 or more panels with caching off no longer rejects one of its own panels.</li>
            <li>Dashboard charts color HTTP status classes by meaning, leave gaps in unstacked areas, and keep value-axis labels distinct.</li>
            <li>MCP <code>translate_logchefql</code> and <code>query_logchefql</code> default to UTC when no timezone is sent.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="contributors">
          <strong>Contributors:</strong> Thanks to <a href="https://github.com/sujay2306" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@sujay2306</a> for requiring source access before a team admin can link a source to a team (<a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/pull/279" target="_blank" rel="noopener">#279</a>). Full details in <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#280---2026-11-22" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="version" id="v2.7.0">
      <div class="version-header">
        <a class="version-tag" href="#v2.7.0">v2.7.0</a>
        <span class="version-date">Nov 15, 2026</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/releases/tag/v2.7.0" class="version-link" target="_blank">Release notes &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="release-kicker">Dashboards that answer the question</p>
      <p class="release-intro">
        <strong>Panels run SQL as written and show the result the way it reads best</strong>: stats with comparisons and sparklines, charts, toplists and tables with rules, across tabs. Time macros let one query follow any range, a query's own <code>LIMIT</code> is respected everywhere, and a result ClickHouse could have cut says so.
      </p>

      <ul class="release-highlights">
        <li><strong>Charts from any result</strong>Map result columns to bars, lines, areas, pies and toplists, with value labels, stacking and exact tooltips.</li>
        <li><strong>Stats that compare</strong>A stat shows the change from the previous row, coloured good or bad, with a sparkline. Thresholds colour values and draw reference lines.</li>
        <li><strong>One query, any range</strong><code>{"{{__time_filter}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__interval}}"}</code> and the other time macros render from the picker in panels, the Explorer, the CLI and MCP.</li>
        <li><strong>No silent cuts</strong>Every result reports whether it was cut and by what. ClickHouse profile limits fail loudly instead of trimming results.</li>
      </ul>

      <aside class="upgrade-note">
        <strong>Before upgrading:</strong> back up the metadata database. Startup runs three migrations on each store (SQLite 000039 to 000041, Postgres 000013 to 000015). Dashboard PUTs must send <code>revision</code>, schema 2 dashboards need the client schema headers, CLI <code>--var</code> values drop their quotes, and ClickHouse alerts whose <code>SETTINGS</code> can stop a query early record an evaluation error until fixed. Reload open tabs after the upgrade. The <a href="https://github.com/mr-karan/logchef/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG</a> lists every upgrade note.
      </aside>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type security">Security</div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Collection links have a kind</strong>: A pin is a bookmark and grants nothing. Only a managed link, which only the query's creator or an admin can make, lets the collection's editors edit the query.</li>
          <li><strong>Stored secrets stay with their endpoint</strong>: A source edit asks for the password or token again when the host, username, TLS setting or base URL changes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type added">Added</div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>Result charts</strong>: Bars, lines, areas, pies and toplists from result columns, with suggested roles and confirmed column kinds.</li>
          <li><strong>Stat comparison and sparklines</strong>, with exact deltas and percentages.</li>
          <li><strong>Thresholds and table rules</strong>: Colour stat values or backgrounds, draw chart reference lines, and colour table cells or rows. Number and time formats per column.</li>
          <li><strong>Tabs and free sizes</strong>: Up to 10 tabs, each with its own grid, and panels from 2 to 12 columns wide and up to 12 rows tall.</li>
          <li><strong>Time macros</strong>: <code>{"{{__time_filter}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__from}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__to}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__interval}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__interval_s}}"}</code>, <code>{"{{__timezone}}"}</code> and <code>{"{{__tz_offset}}"}</code>. A panel can set its own bucket size and its own range, including calendar ranges such as <code>today-6d</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>The <code>day</code> variable</strong>: A date-only picker with <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> literals.</li>
          <li><strong>Safe saves</strong>: Two edits from the same revision cannot overwrite each other. A conflict offers save as copy, overwrite, or load theirs. A banner asks you to reload after a server upgrade.</li>
          <li><strong>Recent activity on ClickHouse views</strong>: Opt in per source, with time, row and byte caps that fail loudly.</li>
          <li><strong>Explorer</strong>: A cell menu to copy or filter, field actions for nested JSON keys in the expanded row, a Wrap toggle, a prefix field in compact view, and Add to query from the loaded-rows search.</li>
          <li><strong>CLI and MCP</strong>: <code>logchef sql --interval</code> and <code>--var</code>. MCP <code>query_logs</code> gains <code>timezone</code>, <code>interval</code> and <code>variables</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type changed">Changed</div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li><strong>The LIMIT rule</strong>: The server returns at most the smallest of the query's own <code>LIMIT</code>, the request limit and the configured maximum, on every surface. Stats report <code>limit_source</code> and <code>truncation</code>, shown as a chip.</li>
          <li><strong>ClickHouse limits fail loudly</strong>: Logchef sends its own result limits and sets every overflow mode to throw, so a profile limit fails the query with an error that names it. A shard that does not answer fails the query.</li>
          <li><strong>Dashboard list</strong>: Summaries instead of panel blobs, so the list loads fast with many dashboards.</li>
          <li><strong>Explorer</strong>: The message column takes the spare width, scanned rows move to the stats strip, LogchefQL errors read as sentences, and Generate SQL appears only in SQL mode.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="change-section">
        <div class="change-type fixed">Fixed</div>
        <ul class="change-list">
          <li>Editing a dashboard starts from the latest saved version, and leaving with unsaved edits asks first.</li>
          <li>A click on a cell expands the row instead of putting the escaped log line into the editor.</li>
          <li>Expanded fields stay open when a query runs, Group By no longer shifts, and Cmd/Ctrl+Enter closes the autocomplete popup.</li>
          <li><code>logchef sql</code> ignores time macros inside comments and never puts its added condition inside a trailing comment.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

